#ASSERT `Is my purchase an eligible owner occupier transaction` `1 Nov 2026` `vacant land` TRUE FALSE TRUE `1 Dec 2026` TRUE EQUALS `under the 2026 determination` (`not eligible` `a transferee acquires other than in their personal capacity (as a trustee, a partner in a partnership or an agent)`)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 8. The residence requirement at its edges (all three determinations). HYPOTHETICAL dates.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- "within 1 year after the residence start date" (30 September 2026): moving in on 30 September 2027 is in time;
-- 1 October 2027 is not.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` `30 Sep 2026` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2027) FALSE `30 Sep 2026` FALSE 0 EQUALS `eligible`
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` `30 Sep 2026` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2027) FALSE `30 Sep 2026` FALSE 0 EQUALS `not eligible` `no transferee occupies the property as their principal place of residence within 1 year after the residence start date`
-- "a continuous period of at least 1 year": moving out on the first anniversary of moving in completes it; the day
-- before does not.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` `30 Sep 2026` TRUE `30 Sep 2026` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS `eligible`
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` `30 Sep 2026` TRUE `30 Sep 2026` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 9 2027) FALSE 0 EQUALS `not eligible` `the occupation does not last for the residence period`
-- "a shorter residence period (including no period)": a period of 0 days is met by any occupation.
#ASSERT `Have I met the residence requirement` `30 Sep 2026` TRUE `30 Sep 2026` TRUE `30 Sep 2026` TRUE 0 EQUALS `eligible`
-- 18 months after 31 August 2026 is read as 29 February 2028 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for a shorter residence period or a later start` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028
-- A year after 29 February 2028 is read as 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2028) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 7 2026) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 7 2025

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 9. The two Tables at their edges (DI2026-155 Tables 1 and 2), and Table 3.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Table 1, first band: $0.28 for every $100 or part: $100 is 0.28; $101 is 2 parts, 0.56; $260,000 is 2,600 parts, 728.
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 100 EQUALS 0.28
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 101 EQUALS 0.56
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 260000 EQUALS 728
-- $260,001: 728 + 2.20 for 1 part = 730.20. Each band's top equals the next band's base: 300,000 gives 728 + 880 =
-- 1,608; 500,000 gives 1,608 + 6,800 = 8,408; 750,000 gives 8,408 + 10,800 = 19,208; 1,000,000 gives 19,208 + 14,750
-- = 33,958; 1,455,000 gives 33,958 + 6.40 x 4,550 = 33,958 + 29,120 = 63,078.
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 260001 EQUALS 730.2
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 300000 EQUALS 1608
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 500000 EQUALS 8408
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 750000 EQUALS 19208
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 1000000 EQUALS 33958
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 1455000 EQUALS 63078
-- NOTES finding 4. Above $1,455,000 the flat $4.54 per $100 on the whole: $1,455,100 x 4.54% = 66,061.54, a jump of
-- 2,983.54 for $100 more. $1,600,000: 72,640.
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 1455100 EQUALS 66061.54
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 1600000 EQUALS 72640
-- NOTES finding 5. The flat rate has no "or part of $100": $1,455,050 x 4.54 / 100 = 6,605,927 / 100 = 66,059.27,
-- unrounded.
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 1455050 EQUALS 66059.27
-- Table 2: 200,000 is 2,000 parts at 1.20 = 2,400; 200,001 is 2,402.20; 300,000 is 4,600; 1,455,000 is 36,950 +
-- 29,120 = 66,070; 1,455,100 is 66,061.54, 8.46 less (NOTES finding 4).
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` 200000 EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` 200001 EQUALS 2402.2
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` 300000 EQUALS 4600
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` 1455000 EQUALS 66070
#ASSERT `What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` 1455100 EQUALS 66061.54
-- The owner occupier saving is 4,600 - 1,608 = 2,992 at every value from $300,000 to $1,455,000 (NOTES finding 4).
#ASSERT (`What is the duty at the rate for other transactions` 900000) MINUS (`What is the duty at the owner occupier rate` 900000) EQUALS 2992
-- Table 3 (pt 3, commercial; not asked from the seat): nil to $2,100,000; above, $5.00 per $100 on the whole: $2,500,000
-- gives 125,000.
#ASSERT `the duty under` `Table 3` `on` 2100000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the duty under` `Table 3` `on` 2500000 EQUALS 125000

-- NOTES finding 3. Neither scheme has a value or income cap: Mia's facts with a $2,000,000 house, and Joan's with a
-- $1,800,000 unit, are still nil.
#ASSERT `the duty for a buyer of a home` `15 Aug 2026` `a home` 2000000 2000000 `30 Sep 2026` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nil duty under the Home Buyer Concession Scheme (DI2026-157 s 7)`
#ASSERT `the duty for a pensioner` `2 Oct 2026` 1800000 `age pension` 72 `lives there before the transaction` `15 Dec 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nil duty under the Pensioner Duty Concession Scheme (DI2026-159 s 9)`

